From 437f302fbf9a473bd9f43296f9f50cd35ea6d1e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:21:30 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op and Longshot's crash reports: nothing sent, co-op's
 lines kept out

A co-op build is not Longshot's to support (owner's decision): it sends
nothing to Longshot's services, files nothing with Longshot and never says it
is a Longshot release. host/hos_crash_dialog.c reads no address (no Report
automatically, no silent send of longshot_crash.ini) and its release flag is
always 0; Report manually saves and copies the report and opens co-op's page
on reporting a problem (host/hos_crash_dialog.h's words, HOS_CRASH_ISSUES);
gpu/vk/perf_report.cpp never starts (no performance summaries);
nx2/addresses.ini has every address empty. The Insert menu's Bug report
(gpu/vk/vk_bug_report.cpp, vk_menu.cpp) points to that page too, not
Longshot's issue form, and Save my pipeline list (Longshot issue 14) is
neither listed nor run.

The reports co-op's players save and send to us leave co-op's own log lines
out (server address, nicknames): the crash report's two readers, crash_lines
and read_log, and the Bug report's copied logs skip a line
host/hos_coop_crash.h calls co-op's ("coop:" or "coop voice:" after hos_log's
tags and the module's level word).
